====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} The colour of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the colour which is evoked by the longest visible [[wavelengths]] (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive colour.
#: {{color panel|FF0000}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Red''' can be seen as hot or angry.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Leah Dolan|title=How the Superman ‘S’ became fashion’s favorite logo|url=https://www.cnn.com/style/superman-costume-fashion|date=2025-02-21|passage=And although we’ve certainly seen a variety of blue shades — from periwinkle to cobalt and even Dean Cain’s indigo-washed costume from the 1990’s TV show “Lois & Clark” — Superman’s uniform is still instantly recognizable across generations. In fact, there is only one film — Zack Snyder’s 2013 “Man of Steel” — in which Superman does not wear his iconic '''red''' belted trunks.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251201074009/https://www.cnn.com/style/superman-costume-fashion|archivedate=1 December 2025}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kristen Rogers|title=Over half of US states are trying to eliminate food dyes. Here’s what you can do now|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/29/health/food-dye-bans-states-wellness|date=2025-03-29|passage='''Red''' No. 3, '''red''' No. 40, blue No. 2 and green No. 3 all have been linked with cancer or tumors in animals. Other sources say '''red''' No. 40 and yellow No. 5 and No. 6 contain or may be contaminated with known carcinogens.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261011090009/https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/29/health/food-dye-bans-states-wellness|archivedate=11 October 2026}}
# {{senseid|en|communist}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[revolutionary]] [[socialist]] or (''most commonly'') a [[Communist]]; {{qualifier|usually capitalized}} a [[Bolshevik]], a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War.
#: {{cot|en|pinko}}
# {{lb|en|countable|snooker}} One of the 15 red balls used in [[snooker]], distinguished from the [[colour]]s.
# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} [[#Adjective|Red]] [[wine]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1977|month=September|title=w:Scenes from an Italian Restaurant|author=w:Billy Joel|album={{w|The Stranger (album)|The Stranger}}|passage=A bottle of '''red''', a bottle of white / It all depends upon your appetite / I'll meet you any time you want / in our Italian restaurant.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Jeffrey P. Landry|title=Temptation Mango
|passage=He produced a wine key from his jacket pocket and effortlessly removed the cork from the bottle of '''red'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2008|month=January–February|title=70 Ways to Improve Every Day of the Week|journal=w:Men's Health|volume=23|issue=1|issn=1054-4836|page={{gbooks|6ccDAAAAMBAJ|135|red}}|passage='''59 {{smallcaps|sneak in some red}}''' Smuggle a bottle of wine, two glasses, and a corkscrew into a long matinee. Red wine is rich in life-extending antioxidants, and the caper will add zest even to a bad movie.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any of several varieties of [[ale]] which are brewed with red or kilned [[malt]], giving the beer a red colour.
#: {{hypo|en|Flanders red|Irish red}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-06-05|author=Howard Stelzer|title=Beer Cocktails: 50 Superbly Crafted Cocktails that Liven Up Your Lagers and Ales|publisher=Harvard Common Press|isbn=9781558328006
|text=American '''reds''' and doppelbocks are heavy lagers as well. It really comes down to how the beer was made. Beyond that, brewers are immensely creative and have developed styles of both ale and lager that run a wide range of attributes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2016-04-01|author=Lonely Planet; Helena Smith; Andy Symington; Donna Wheeler|title=Lonely Planet Belgium & Luxembourg|publisher=Lonely Planet|isbn=9781760341367
|text=No other country has a brewing tradition as richly diverse as that of Belgium, with beers ranging from pleasant pale lagers to wild, winelike Flemish '''reds''' and lambics.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal}} A red variety of an animal, such as a [[red kangaroo]] or a [[red squirrel]].
# {{lb|en|countable|informal|UK|birdwatching}} A [[redshank]].
# {{lb|en|derogatory|offensive}} An [[American Indian]].
#: {{syn|en|redskin}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} The drug [[secobarbital]]; a capsule of this drug.
#: {{syn|en|redbird|red devil}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1970|title=Truckin'|artist=Grateful Dead|album=American Beauty|passage=What in the world ever became of sweet Jane? / She lost her sparkle, you know she isn't the same / Livin' on '''reds''', vitamin C, and cocaine}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author=Hunter S. Thompson|title=Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas|publisher=Harper Perennial|year_published=2005|page=202|passage=The big market, these days, is in Downers. '''Reds''' and smack—Seconal and heroin—and a hellbroth of bad domestic grass sprayed with everything from arsenic to horse tranquillizers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|year_published=2021|author=w:Jeffery Deaver|title=w:The Coffin Dancer|location=New York, NY|publisher=w:Pocket Books|isbn=9781982163792|page={{gbooks|dWsREAAAQBAJ|285|reds}}|passage=“Whatchu got, man?” / “'''Reds''', bennies, dexies, yellow jackets, demmies.” / “Yeah, demmies're good shit, man. I pay you. Fuck. I got money. I'm hurting inside. Got beat up. Where my money?”}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[red light]] {{gloss|a traffic signal}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1974|author=Tom Waits|title=(Looking for) The Heart of Saturday Night|url=http://www.tomwaits.com/songs/song/329/Looking_For_The_Heart_Of_Saturday_Night/|album=w:The Heart of Saturday Night|text=Stopping on the '''red''', you're going on the green / Cause tonight will be like nothing you've ever seen / And you're barreling down the boulevard / You're looking for the heart of Saturday night}}
# {{lb|en|Ireland|UK|beverages|informal}} {{cap|red lemonade}}
# {{lb|en|particle physics}} One of the three [[color charge]]s for [[quark]]s.
# {{lb|en|US|colloquial|uncountable}} {{cap|chili con carne}} {{q|usually in the phrase "bowl of red"}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1982|journal=The Rotarian|volume=140|issue=1|page=39
|passage=Houston visited a home in an early pioneer settlement where he was offered a bowl of '''red'''. Houston eagerly took his first large spoonful. His eyes watering, he spat out his bite {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} The [[redfish]] or [[red drum]], {{taxlink|Sciaenops ocellatus|species}}, a fish with reddish fins and scales.
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2013|month=November|author=Catch Cormier|title=Sightcasting for redfish|work=Louisiana Sportsman|url=https://www.louisianasportsman.com/fishing/inshore-fishing/pumpkin-time/|passage=The species Sciaenops ocellatus certainly isn’t lacking for nicknames.{{...}} Clear water also favors sightcasting. Against the dark background of marsh mud, a '''red''' will appear like a pumpkin — big, orange and round.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251117131605/https://www.louisianasportsman.com/fishing/inshore-fishing/pumpkin-time/|archivedate=17 November 2025}}
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[tomato|Tomato]] [[ketchup]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Jon Bounds; Danny Smith|title=Pier Review: A Road Trip in Search of the Great British Seaside
|passage=I squeeze some '''red''' out over my chips and feel guilty. Nothing is as English as Heinz ketchup in the sauce game, except perhaps HP.}}
# A red dye or pigment.
# A pen, pencil, crayon, etc., made of red pigment.
# Something, or a part of a thing, which is red.

